        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #E3DFD8;color:#2F3438;font-weight:500;">150 ft of pine or cedar, installed total</td>
          <td style="padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #E3DFD8;color:#2A3035;font-weight:700;white-space:nowrap;">Pine $2,200-$3,300; cedar $3,000-$4,500 (TX Fence & Deck)</td>
          <td style="padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #E3DFD8;color:#555;">That firm says cedar typically costs 20 to 35 percent more in materials.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding:13px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #E3DFD8;color:#2F3438;font-weight:500;">Board-on-board upgrade</td>
